WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.093
SIEM platforms are powerful, but they are not magic.

2
00:00:03.093 --> 00:00:09.738
Poorly configured SIEM environments may generate excessive false positives or fail to detect important activity.

3
00:00:09.738 --> 00:00:15.585
Collecting too much data without prioritization can overwhelm analysts and increase noise.

4
00:00:15.585 --> 00:00:18.190
Missing data sources create blind spots.

5
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.710
Correlation rules require maintenance and refinement as environments change.

6
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:31.879
A useful alert today may become noisy after an application update, while a new cloud service may need new log sources and detection logic.

7
00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:38.754
Organizations also need trained personnel who understand how to investigate alerts and improve detections over time.

8
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:44.351
SIEM technology supports security operations, but people and processes remain essential.

9
00:00:44.351 --> 00:00:50.039
The value comes from thoughtful configuration, ongoing tuning, and disciplined investigation.
